{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"texture mapping in open gl texture mapping in open gl","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","fileName":"Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Texture Mapping in OpenGL","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[OpenGL Rendering Pipeline]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OpenGL Rendering Pipeline","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"texture mapping in open gl texture mapping in open gl","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","fileName":"Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Texture Mapping in OpenGL","heading":"Texture Mapping in OpenGL","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Texture mapping in OpenGL associates vertex texture coordinates with an image stored in a texture object. Rasterization interpolates the coordinates across a triangle, and the fragment shader samples the image to determine surface color or another material value.\n\nThe texture must be uploaded with a known format and bound to the sampler expected by the shader. Filtering and wrapping rules define how samples behave between texels or outside the basic coordinate range.","tags":["baby"],"links":["OpenGL Rendering Pipeline","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Mapping in OpenGL.md","sourceType":"markdown","